    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0655" n="1489" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/451</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-13T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 13, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10022. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 572. Your 466, Department’s 7707, May 12, 2.45 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >May 11, 7 p.m.</hi>] I am informed that there is some prospect of the Dutch
                    being willing to reopen negotiations for a general agreement and have asked the
                    Foreign Office what news they have on this point. If this proves to be the case
                    think it would be unwise to start independent negotiations regarding Dutch
                    colonial trade. The Foreign <pb facs="0656" n="1490" xml:id="pg1490"/> Office
                    has suggested that I telegraph you asking that you give no definite declaration
                    in regard to future requisitioning of Dutch ships without consultation with
                    them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
